// sokuji-native: ggml allocates this KV cache uninitialised, and every decode step
// attends all cache_steps slots of it (the flash attention at :659); the slots not
// yet written are masked by a finite -10000 (fill_t3_decode_attention_mask,
// :697-710), which ggml's CPU flash attention does not skip: it skips only an exact
// -INFINITY (ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:8968 at ggml 0.26.0). A fresh mmap reads as zeros and
// is harmless, but heap memory recycled from a model that ran earlier in the same
// process can hold huge or non-finite values, which can turn the logits to NaN: T3
// then emits no speech token ("HiFT mel shape mismatch") or silently different
// speech. Zero the cache once, as upstream's crisperwhisper does for its own KV
// tensors (models/crisperwhisper/whisper_runtime.cpp:290-291). A mask change upstream
// would not make this redundant: ggml-vulkan's flash attention lets an unwritten slot
// through even under an exact -INFINITY mask (shown at op level on the fork's ggml and
// on 0.26.0 alike), and only the zeroed cache covers both backends.
for (const auto & layer : key_cache_tensors_) {
